    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E66B3C1689D7CACD88837E5AD889588C/jobs/939075": {
      "title": "COM Lab Instructor, OMM",
      "description": "COM Lab Instructor, OMM You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account COM Lab Instructor, OMM Hattiesburg - Hattiesburg, MS 39401 Apply Apply Description Job Summary The primary duty of a Lab Instructor is assisting the WCUCOM faculty in lab-related courses at the graduate, medical school level. Duties and Responsibilities Participate in Osteopathic Principles and Practices lab, teach/discuss/answer student questions Lecture as needed as it relates to specialty Provide grading resources for CSA’s Qualifications Physical Demands Must possess the physical ability to actively facilitate student learning in the lab setting for extended period of times Must have vision to read printed materials and a computer screen; hearing and speech to communicate in person and over the telephone Must have the ability to sit or stand for extended periods of time Required Application Documents Cover Letter Vitae Qualifications Required Qualifications A graduate of a college or school of medicine accredited by the Commission on Osteopathic College Accreditation (COCA) Experience in family medicine, general practice, or equivalent training Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
